    "answer": {
      "short": "$y'=-\\dfrac{2xy}{1+x^2}$. Correct answer: D.",
      "worked": "At $(1,1)$, the field has a negative gradient, eliminating A and B.\n\nAt $(-4,1)$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Option C: }y'&=-\\frac{2(-4)(1)}{1+1^2}\\\\&=4\\\\\\text{Option D: }y'&=-\\frac{2(-4)(1)}{1+(-4)^2}\\\\&=\\frac{8}{17}.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe segment at $(-4,1)$ rises at an angle less than $45^\\circ$ to the positive $x$-axis, so its gradient is between $0$ and $1$. This agrees with $\\frac{8}{17}$.\n\nCorrect answer: D.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
